# GitHub delivery

Follow `docs/engineering/github-cicd.md`.

- Protect default and production branches and require peer approval plus all
  applicable checks.
- Use least-privilege workflow permissions, pinned action SHAs, timeouts, and
  concurrency controls.
- Use GitHub OpenID Connect for short-lived AWS access. Do not store long-lived
  AWS keys.
- Never expose secrets to untrusted pull-request workflows.
- Build once, scan, identify artifacts immutably, and promote the same artifact
  through environments.
- Keep development, staging, and production isolated.
- Rehearse migrations and rollback in staging and protect production with
  manual approval.
- Use reviewed infrastructure-as-code.
- Shell scripts use Bash strict mode, quoted expansions, validated input,
  meaningful exit codes, and ShellCheck.
- Every release records artifacts, migrations, approvals, checks, owner,
  verification, and rollback evidence.
